HHIISSTTOORRYY
       SVID 2.

       Because of historical variations in behavior across systems, this
       function is not specified in any recent standard.

       4.2BSD had a ggaammmmaa() that computed ln(|Gamma(|_x|)|), leaving the sign
       of Gamma(|_x|) in the external integer _s_i_g_n_g_a_m.  In 4.3BSD the name was
       changed to llggaammmmaa(3), and the man page promises

           "At some time in the future the name gamma will be rehabilitated
           and used for the Gamma function"

       This did indeed happen in 4.4BSD, where ggaammmmaa() computes the Gamma
       function (with no effect on _s_i_g_n_g_a_m).  However, this came too late, and
       we now have ttggaammmmaa(3), the "true gamma" function.

